# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_worker_event_timeout.py" "WORKER EVENT-TIMEOUT GATE: PASS" "one poison tenant cannot multiply GitHub retries and EventQueue retries into a 787-second single-worker stall" "WORKER EVENT-TIMEOUT: one monotonic delivery budget covers GitHub attempts and every EventQueue attempt, while a positive GitHub Retry-After/reset becomes an attempt-neutral durable not_before schedule instead of an in-worker sleep. A real 429 Retry-After:60 runs only once through DeliveryStore plus EventQueue, tenant B starts immediately with a fresh deadline, and an overdue processor return is never recorded as success. The real trickling-socket proof remains, so body and header reads are bounded as well." "worker event-timeout: the formerly multiplicative 5x GitHub by 3x worker retry path is scheduled once per delivery; another account drains next instead of waiting roughly 787 seconds" 24
